{
  "_comment": [
    "Span nodes exactly as Phoenix GraphQL returns them to navigator.js",
    "(`attributes` is the JSON string Phoenix serializes, nested/unflattened;",
    "`parentId` is the parent's OTel span id, null on roots).",
    "",
    "talon_trace models a real Talon run (producer: kestrel-talon",
    "observability.py): the run ROOT carries kestrel.agent_name=='talon' and",
    "kestrel.run_id; each STAGE span is opened as start_span(<stage>) — so it is",
    "NAMED by its stage — alongside an immediately-ended '<stage> (started)'",
    "twin (#80), and carries kestrel.stage plus the worker-naming agent_name",
    "('talon/implement', 'talon/review', else 'talon'). The OpenInference kind is",
    "chosen PER STAGE, not per role: implement/review are LLM, coordinate AGENT,",
    "gate CHAIN — so nothing may key off a stage span's kind. Event/tool children",
    "(command_execution, Bash, self-review) inherit the same kestrel.stage, which",
    "is why the stage token alone never identifies a stage bar; agent_response",
    "shows the other stamping the worker split must survive — a prefixed",
    "agent_name with NO kestrel.stage at all. NO talon span stamps",
    "kestrel.session_id or session.id; the run id is the only session identity.",
    "",
    "emitter_session models a hook.py session: root marker + summary carry",
    "kestrel.session_id; the tool child carries the agent name only."
  ],
